From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 12:03:36 -0500
Subject: feat: a playing video pops out when its tab is left (S-95)

With Settings > Stedding > Pages and menus > "Pop out a playing video
when you leave its tab" on, off by default, leaving a tab whose page
plays a video with sound puts the video in picture in picture, as the
picture-in-picture key does, and showing the tab again puts it back in
the page, playing on (docs/features/player.md Mp2, Mp4; settings T61).
A muted or paused video, sound alone and a split's other pane on screen
are not left. The command bar has the switch, and "mini player" finds
it (Mp6).

Why: GitHub discussion 104, Arc's mini player. Chromium's automatic
picture in picture waits for a Safe Browsing check of the page, and
Stedding has no Safe Browsing (BACKLOG S-75), so it never fired for an
ordinary video.
Removable when: never; Stedding's own player. Mp1 moves the video into
the window's card in place of Chromium's window.
